										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Binance Wallet has a new competition running. NES perpetuals, $50,000 on the table, ten days to trade your way into a share of it.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Window opens July 28 at 13:00 UTC. Closes August 7, same time.</span></p>
<h2><b>What Is NES?</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Nesa is a Layer-1 blockchain. The pitch: decentralized AI inference that actually stays private. Models run across distributed compute nodes instead of a central server, and the outputs are cryptographically verifiable the whole way through. No single operator sitting in the middle reading everything.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">NES handles three things inside that system: inference query fees, node operator staking, governance votes.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Mainnet launched May 9, 2026. Hard cap of 1 billion tokens. Binance Alpha listed it June 24, running a Wallet booster campaign alongside.</span></p>
