					<description><![CDATA[<p>Claros Raises Funding To Scale Global PFAS Solutions  Claros Technologies announced $55 Million in funding to scale commercially and eliminate PFAS solutions.To facilitate increased manufacturing, enhanced operations, and expansion of</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/claros-raises-55m-series-b-pfas-destruction/" data-wpel-link="internal">Claros Raises $55M to Accelerate PFAS Destruction Technology</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Claros Raises Funding To Scale Global PFAS Solutions </b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Claros Technologies announced $55 Million in funding to scale commercially and eliminate PFAS solutions.To facilitate increased manufacturing, enhanced operations, and expansion of the company’s PFAS destruction technology in North America, Europe, and Asia, along with further research and development efforts. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Treehouse Family Capital LLC, in collaboration with Daikin America, Veralto, Bush Foundation, Nord Asset Management, Saint Paul &amp; Minnesota Foundation, and its existing investors led the funding round. Today’s announcement enables Claros Technology to execute its next global growth strategies.</span></p>
<h2><b>Claros Expands Commercial Deployment Of PFAS Technology</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company also plans to grow ClarosLabs, its analytical services division, as industries seek reliable PFAS testing and permanent destruction solutions. Claros has positioned itself as a provider of integrated PFAS mitigation solutions. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Our own ClarosTechUV system permanently destroys long-chain, short-chain, and ultra-short-chain PFAS compounds by permanently eradicating contaminants &#8211; rather than just transporting contaminants between waste streams. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The technology serves industrial manufacturers, environmental remediation firms, consulting companies, utilities, and government organisations worldwide today. The funding will significantly expand engineering and manufacturing operations while accelerating global market adoption among industrial clients. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">ClarosTech also plans to increase hiring across commercial and technical teams while strengthening customer support capabilities. The company will continue investing in application development to support growing customer demand and commercial deployment globally. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Chief executive officer and co-founder Michelle Bellanca said ClarosTech has transitioned from technology validation to commercial success.  She explained that successful industrial and environmental projects have demonstrated the effectiveness of the platform at scale.</span></p>
<h2><b>Technology Addresses Growing Environmental Regulations</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_203788" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203788" class="size-full wp-image-203788" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Claros-2.png" alt="Illustration of PFAS destruction technology treating contaminated water, combining environmental remediation systems with laboratory analysis and regulatory compliance monitoring." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-203788" class="wp-caption-text">Advanced PFAS destruction technology is helping organisations address stricter environmental regulations by combining permanent chemical removal, precise laboratory analysis, and scalable remediation solutions for industrial and public health applications. Source: Created by Ventureburn.</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Demand for permanent PFAS destruction is increasing as governments tighten environmental standards. Earlier this year, the technology also demonstrated similar performance during large-scale groundwater remediation projects.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">European regulators continue advancing restrictions under the proposed REACH framework, while U.S. federal and state agencies are expanding drinking water rules, industrial discharge requirements, and remediation programmes.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Claros believes organisations now require both reliable destruction technology and accurate laboratory analysis to meet </span><a href="https://www.lawinsider.com/dictionary/compliance-obligations" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">compliance obligations</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400">. Alongside its destruction platform, ClarosLabs provides accredited PFAS detection, quantification, and exposure assessment services.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company highlighted several recent milestones that strengthened investor confidence. In late 2025, Claros partnered with Daikin America to complete one of the world&#8217;s largest industrial PFAS destruction demonstrations, achieving more than 99.99% destruction across targeted PFAS compounds. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: <a href="https://ventureburn.com/prophetx-raises-35m-funding/" data-wpel-link="internal">ProphetX Raises $35M to Expand Federally Regulated Sports Prediction Market</a></span></p>
<h2><b>Funding Supports Global Expansion And Manufacturing</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The latest financing reflects growing confidence in environmental technologies that combine scientific innovation with commercial scalability. Investors believe Claros has reached an important stage where its focus shifts from validating the technology to deploying it broadly across multiple industries.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Treehouse Family Capital Manager Jack Cogen said Claros has demonstrated that its integrated destruction and analytical platform performs effectively under real-world conditions. The company is ideally suited to gain traction from a strong regulatory trend and to meet a growing global market&#8217;s desire for permanent PFAS solutions.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Claros, founded in 2018 in Minneapolis, develops technologies to eliminate PFAS permanently for industries in semiconductor manufacturing, aerospace, pharmaceuticals, and the healthcare industries that, he noted, need to find alternative ways to handle those chemicals moving forward.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/claros-raises-55m-series-b-pfas-destruction/" data-wpel-link="internal">Claros Raises $55M to Accelerate PFAS Destruction Technology</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
