		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://ventureburn.com/?p=203783</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In a major move to protect enterprise networks, Hush Security raises $30M in a Series A funding round. Strategic investor Akamai Technologies joined existing backers Battery Ventures and YL Ventures</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/hush-security-raises-30m-ai-agent-governance-gap/" data-wpel-link="internal">Hush Security Raises $30 Million To Close the Governance Gap for AI Agent </a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400">In a major move to protect enterprise networks, Hush Security raises $30M in a </span><a href="https://www.hush.security/resources/hush-security-raises-30m-to-close-the-ai-agent-governance-gap-with-akamai-joining-as-strategic-investor/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">Series A</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> funding round. Strategic investor Akamai Technologies joined existing backers Battery Ventures and YL Ventures to support the company. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Less than a year after emerging from stealth, Hush has raised $41 million in total capital to redefine non-human identity security. The fresh investment comes at a pivotal moment for enterprise cybersecurity teams. Autonomous software tools now carry out complex tasks inside core corporate infrastructure. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Gartner predicts the average Fortune 500 company will run over 150,000 AI agents by 2028, up from fewer than 15 last year. Yet, recent research from Omdia reveals that 96% of organizations still operate on legacy governance frameworks. These older tools cannot properly govern autonomous digital workers.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Extending Identity Security to Autonomous AI Agents</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Hush Security treats identity as the core control point for non-human identities and AI agents. Traditional enterprise security relies heavily on static API keys and permanent system credentials. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Hush replaces these vulnerable methods with dynamic access controls designed specifically for automated software workflows. This shift eliminates long-term credential leaks.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The platform creates a secure, sanctioned pathway for AI agents operating across enterprise environments. Every agent registers in a central catalog that strips away standing credentials. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Instead, Hush grants scoped, just-in-time access right when an agent performs a specific action. System administrators track every action in real time and maintain a centralized kill switch to stop suspicious operations instantly.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/multiverse-computing-raises-570-million-for-expansion/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Multiverse Computing Raises $570M for Global Expansion</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Core Pillars of Hush Security</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To streamline security management, Hush structures its platform around three core operational pillars:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Discover: Identifies all managed AI agents, desktop assistants, and hidden shadow tools across the business.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Control: Enforces least-privilege rules, manages just-in-time access, and provides immediate kill-switch capabilities.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Audit: Logs every agent decision to deliver complete visibility for regulatory compliance and security audits.</span></li>
</ul>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Enterprise Adoption and Strategic Backing</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Global enterprise organizations are already integrating Hush into their daily operational workflows. Kyndryl, the world’s largest IT infrastructure services provider, deployed Hush internally to protect its global operations. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Beyond internal deployment, Kyndryl partnered with Hush to resell the identity platform directly to its enterprise clients worldwide. Akamai Technologies joined the Series A round to address identity challenges across autonomous software networks. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Akamai leadership emphasized that every major internet evolution requires a fresh security approach. They view identity management as the critical security gateway required to protect expanding AI workloads.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Early investors Battery Ventures and YL Ventures also expanded their financial backing in this round. Both investment firms noted that static secrets create severe enterprise risks. As companies give software agents real authority over core data, securing those non-human identities becomes vital for business continuity. This ensures companies scale AI safely.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates:</i></b> <a href="https://ventureburn.com/ropedia-raises-30m-pre-a-funding-scale-physical-ai-infrastructure/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Ropedia Raises $30M To Scale Physical AI Data Infrastructure</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Expanding US Footprint and Product Integrations</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Hush Security was created by the founding team behind Meta Networks, an enterprise security company acquired by Proofpoint in 2019. They bring deep cybersecurity experience. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The founders built Hush specifically to resolve the security gaps created by unmonitored digital credentials and automated non-human identities. The company will direct its $30 million funding toward expanding engineering and sales teams, focusing primarily on rapid growth within the United States market.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Additionally, Hush plans to deepen integrations with major enterprise identity management platforms, accelerate strategic corporate partnerships, and expand native support across popular enterprise AI tools.</span></p>
